  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "AVHRR Sea Surface Temperatures of Northern Gulf of Alaska and Eastern Bering Sea",
  "description": "Time series of hourly sea surface temperatures (SST) using the Advanced Very High Resolution Radiometer (AVHRR) sensor, which orbits the Earth approximately 14 times each day. The images used are of one kilometer resolution. Coverage area includes the northern Gulf of Alaska and eastern Bering Sea. A Sea-Air-Land Modeling and Observing Network (SALMON) Project.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To map sea surface temperatures.",
